  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FPT">Lemma <span data-tag="0FPT">21.48.5</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. The derived category $D(\mathcal{O})$ is a symmetric monoidal category with tensor product given by derived tensor product with usual associativity and commutativity constraints (for sign rules, see More on Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/0FNG" data-tag="0FNG">15.74</a>). </p>
